<volume>15</volume>:<fpage>2899</fpage>&#x02013;2907.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9416833</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><citation citation-type="journal">Kitayama, H., Y. Sugimoto, T. Matsuzaki, Y. Ikawa, and M. Noda. <year>1989</year>. A ras-related gene with transformation suppressor activity. <source>Cell.</source> <volume>56</volume>:<fpage>77</fpage>&#x02013;84.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2642744</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib22"><citation citation-type="journal">Knox, A.L., and N.H. Brown. <year>2002</year>. Rap1 GTPase regulation of adherens junction positioning and cell adhesion. <source>Science.</source> <volume>295</volume>:<fpage>1285</fpage>&#x02013;1288.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11847339</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib23"><citation citation-type="journal">Mammen, A.L., R.L. Huganir, and R.J. O'Brien. <year>1997</year>. Redistribution and stabilization of cell surface glutamate receptors during synapse formation. <source>J. Neurosci.</source> <volume>17</volume>:<fpage>7351</fpage>&#x02013;7358.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9295381</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib24"><citation citation-type="journal">Maridonneau-Parini, I., and J. de Gunzburg. <year>1992</year>. Association of rap1 and rap2 proteins with the specific granules of human neutrophils. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>267</volume>:<fpage>6396</fpage>&#x02013;6402.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1556142</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib25"><citation citation-type="journal">Meng, J., and P.J. Casey. <year>2002</year>. Activation of Gz attenuates Rap1-mediated differentiation of PC12 cells. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>277</volume>:<fpage>43417</fpage>&#x02013;43424.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12198116</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib26"><citation citation-type="journal">Michaelson, D., J. Silletti, G. Murphy, P. D'Eustachio, M. Rush, and M.R. Philips. <year>2001</year>. Differential localization of Rho GTPases in live cells: regulation by hypervariab